6.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.000315569468387622,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":49.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004742745285623399,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.27118,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"MSC Industrial Direct Co., Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the distribution of metalworking and maintenance, repair, and operations (MRO) products and services in the United States, Canada, Mexico, the United Kingdom, and internationally. The company offers metalworking and MRO products, including cutting tools, abrasives, machining fluids, measuring instruments, machinery and accessories, tooling components, fasteners, flat stock, raw materials, machinery hand and power tools, safety and janitorial supplies, plumbing supplies, materials handling products, power transmission components and electrical supplies, as well as stock-keeping units. It serves individual machine shops, companies, and manufacturers, as well as federal agencies, state governments, and public sector healthcare providers. The company was founded in 1941 and is headquartered in Melville, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Martina  McIsaac | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $586K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["MSC Industrial Direct Company,  is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.6B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 8% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 43%.","The business throws off $225M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.38\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 15\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 27% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 55% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5544646602127258},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 87% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $29.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","22 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Financial quality scores above most Industrials peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MSC Industrial Direct (MSM) Stock Looks Reasonably Priced As Cash Flow Supports It","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-msm/msc-industrial-direct/news/msc-industrial-direct-msm-stock-looks-reasonably-priced-as-c","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794558360.131,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.938,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(MSM) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/150/MSM_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_111226023002_1794511802.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794511802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"New South Capital Management Inc. Sells 151,928 Shares of MSC Industrial Direct Company, Inc. $MSM","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/new-south-capital-management-inc-sells-151928-shares-of-msc-industrial-direct-company-inc-msm.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482255.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MSC Industrial Direct (MSM) Pulls 